  "details": "Control characters such as Carriage Return cannot be typed into Char node values.\n\nFor example, if a user wanted to remove control characters (such as a carriage return sign) from a string, the only way to get those values into an array is to parse them from \"ConvertFromUtf32\" and know that char's index.\n\nChar nodes only allow for a single character in the slot, so typing in characters such as \\r and \\n do not work, as they require multiple characters typed in.\n\nHere is a post on this issue from what I believe is the release day of the first early access public build of Udon, which is why I'm making a fully new post:\n\nhttps://feedback.vrchat.com/vrchat-udon-closed-alpha-bugs/p/character-constvariable-nodes-do-not-allow-for-escape-characters",
